filterByCoverage is just a convenience function. You can do all kinds of row filtering on methylKit objects using [] notation.

for example if you want to remove rows from a methylBase object based on coverage of 1st and 2nd sample, you can do the following:

library(methylKit)
data(methylKit)

methylBase.obj

new.obj=methylBase.obj[methylBase.obj$coverage1> 100 & methylBase.obj$coverage2>100 ,]
new.obj

Best,
Altuna

